  "lines": [
    {
      "text": "Birmingham's tap water comes from Wales.",
      "gap": 0.3,
      "caps": [
        "*BIRMINGHAM'S WATER",
        "COMES FROM *WALES"
      ],
      "scene": {
        "type": "map",
        "cam": [
          -2.7,
          52.4,
          9000
        ],
        "pins": [
          [
            "ELAN VALLEY",
            -3.57,
            52.27,
            null
          ],
          [
            "BIRMINGHAM",
            -1.89,
            52.48,
            null
          ]
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "It starts in the Elan Valley, in the hills of mid Wales.",
      "gap": 0.3,
      "caps": [
        "IT *STARTS",
        "IN THE *ELAN VALLEY",
        "MID *WALES"
      ],
      "scene": {
        "type": "map",
        "cam": [
          -3.3,
          52.35,
          13000
        ],
        "pins": [
          [
            "ELAN VALLEY",
            -3.57,
            52.27,
            null
          ]
        ],
        "title": "ELAN VALLEY · MID WALES"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Then it travels seventy-three miles, through a Victorian aqueduct.",
      "gap": 0.3,
      "caps": [
        "*73 MILES",
        "A VICTORIAN *AQUEDUCT"
      ],
      "scene": {
        "type": "stat",
        "tag": "INSTITUTION OF CIVIL ENGINEERS",
        "items": [
          {
            "v": "73",
            "suffix": " mi",
            "l": "ELAN AQUEDUCT · 118 KM",
            "red": true
          }
        ],
        "source": "ICE"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "And there isn't a single pumping station on the way.",
      "gap": 0.25,
      "caps": [
        "NOT A *SINGLE",
        "PUMPING *STATION"
      ],
      "scene": {
        "type": "card",
        "tag": "INSTITUTION OF CIVIL ENGINEERS",
        "l1": "NO PUMPS",
        "l2": "GRAVITY ONLY",
        "source": "ICE"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "It runs on gravity alone, dropping just fifty-two metres the whole way.",
      "gap": 0.3,
      "caps": [
        "*GRAVITY ALONE",
        "JUST *52 METRES",
        "THE WHOLE *WAY"
      ],
      "scene": {
        "type": "stat",
        "tag": "ELAN VALLEY TRUST",
        "items": [
          {
            "v": "52",
            "suffix": " m",
            "l": "TOTAL DROP · WALES TO BIRMINGHAM",
            "red": true
          }
        ],
        "source": "ELAN VALLEY TRUST"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "So the water takes about three days to reach Birmingham.",
      "gap": 0.3,
      "caps": [
        "ABOUT *3 DAYS",
        "TO REACH *BIRMINGHAM"
      ],
      "scene": {
        "type": "stat",
        "tag": "ELAN VALLEY TRUST",
        "items": [
          {
            "v": "3",
            "suffix": " days",
            "l": "WALES TO BIRMINGHAM",
            "red": true
          }
        ],
        "source": "ELAN VALLEY TRUST"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "King Edward the Seventh opened the dams in nineteen-oh-four, and it still flows today.",
      "gap": 0.3,
      "caps": [
        "KING *EDWARD VII",
        "OPENED IT IN *1904",
        "IT STILL *FLOWS"
      ],
      "scene": {
        "type": "card",
        "tag": "ELAN VALLEY TRUST · SEVERN TRENT",
        "l1": "OPENED 1904",
        "l2": "STILL FLOWING",
        "source": "ELAN VALLEY TRUST, SEVERN TRENT"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "And Severn Trent describes this water from Wales as moderately soft.",
      "gap": 0.3,
      "caps": [
        "SEVERN TRENT *SAYS",
        "MODERATELY *SOFT"
      ],
      "scene": {
        "type": "card",
        "tag": "OFFICIAL · SEVERN TRENT",
        "l1": "WATER FROM WALES",
        "l2": "MODERATELY SOFT",
        "source": "SEVERN TRENT"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Where does your water come from? Comment your town.",
      "gap": 0.2,
      "caps": [
        "WHERE DOES *YOURS",
        "COME FROM?",
        "COMMENT YOUR *TOWN"
      ],
      "scene": {
        "type": "cta",
        "title": "COMMENT YOUR TOWN"
      }
    }
  ],
